[[ch04-introduction-unending-frontier]]

== Introduction: Unending Frontier

I'm old enough to have experienced watching Star Trek and the Moon Landing in that order. It was very exciting for a young boy growing up in the late 60s and 70s.

Space, the final frontier. These are the voyages of the starship Enterprise. Its five year mission to seek out new life; new civilizations; to boldly go where no one has gone before.

What is New Democracy? It is an unending frontier.

Society, the unending frontier. These are the voyages of all life. With unending missions to seek out new ways of life; new innovations of civilization; to boldly go where no one has gone before with unending new social organization.


When we read books we do so with a certain purpose and frame of mind. Sometimes that frame of mind is entertainment. Sometimes that frame of mind is education. Sometimes that frame of mind is political, a mind that asks the questions about what kind of society we want to live in.

What frame of mind should one read this book? Frontier. One should be in a frontier frame of mind. A frame of mind seeking out adventure and all that comes with it like risk and danger. A frame to seek out a new life of improved society and all the change that requires. Engineering. Engineering is not an ideology. Engineering is meant to be cherry-picked, parts innovated and replaced based upon experimentation. Ideology is static, never innovates, and must be taken as a whole, i.e. religion. Responsibility. Any society of, by and for the people means imposed responsibility, not rugged individualism. America is founded on a mindset of rugged individualism which is minimal social responsibility. This book is about maximal responsibility in order to be of, by and for the people. Political. What kind of society do you want to belong too? Action. Everyone reading this book should be of the mindset of what actions to take after reading this book.


Let's expand on Engineering. Engineering is about designing parts that fit into a whole design. For example, the wheel is an important part of engineering. Tires on cars have changed many times since the car was invented. That's engineering. Engineering is the opposite of ideology. Ideology makes claims that are unproven and if the outcome of the claims are not realized then the people are at fault. By contrast, in Engineering if the wheel falls off then it is the engineering that is at fault. When thinking in an engineering mindset then one needs to be thinking about the parts within an overall design. Further one needs to think about the design itself.

I encourage you to disagree with and improve on every aspect of the design and parts of New Democracy. That's the nature of an engineering mindset.  Below I'm going to list some of the parts of New Democracy for your engineering consideration and introduction to New Democracy.

New Democracy Design parts:

1. Everyone in. This part addresses a defect in human nature: jealousy and selfishness. Everyone in as a part leaves no one behind no matter how limited that person may be, how evil that person may be.
2. Unending frontier. This part requires life to continue until the End of the Universe. The heat death of the Universe. This will require unending frontiers that expand into the Solar system, the Milky Way galaxy, and all galaxies of the Universe. Religion is the mortal enemy of unending frontier as religion is founded on life ending and life being solely the providence of Earth.
3. Mesh society. Mesh society is a part that requires social organization to be divided into two distinct design parts: mesh nodes and the mesh.
4. Mesh nodes. Mesh nodes are of fixed size. The Irreni design calls for this size to be thirty people. The mesh is composed of mesh nodes being connected by common objectives called projects.
5. Mesh projects. Mesh projects are what connects mesh nodes. Projects are contracts. Contracts are not enforced, but rather measured for results meeting contract objectives.
6. Social innovation. This part requires constant iteration. To this end mesh projects are limited to a maximum of five year duration upon which the contract is either renewed or abandoned based on the mesh nodes remaining in the contract or leaving it.
7. Long-term planning. This part requires multi-generational plans. These plans can span centuries and millennia as will be required to manage Earth, the Solar system and explore the Milky Way galaxy.
8. Unending experimentation society. There are too many variables in life to ever know precisely how to build perfect systems. This means unending frontiers will require unending experimentation. Project contracts that connect mesh nodes are experiments with stated objectives. These objectives are measured where needed in order to establish effectiveness. This effectiveness is a primary factor when deciding to  renew project contracts every five years.
9. Survival society. Mesh nodes are micro-governing organizations, or MGOs, of fixed size thirty people. These MGOs can govern under any structure they choose, including hierarchy and theocracy. However, they must meet survival objectives. These include a year's supply of food, water, electricity and other survival needs. The MGO is in effect a virtual spaceship that can sustain without any dependency on external entities. This survival design gives Mesh Democracy the optimal survival design for large scale disasters such as pandemics, asteroid collisions, and so on.
10. Managed society. Mesh nodes join necessary efforts for survival at larger scales such as managing climate by joining mesh projects. These projects demand MGOs fall under membership management. This is equivalent to modern day human rights. Tyrannical MGOs will not be allowed to join a mesh. Tyrannical meshes are incoherent as a concept as they will collapse to one hierarchy.
11. Voluntary society. Mesh node membership is voluntary. Mesh project contract membership is voluntary. There does not exist any notion of nation of birth. In order to realize commitments then mesh node membership is also contractual. Typically the mesh node contract is for the same length of maximum project contract length of five years.
12. Dependency responsibility. New Democracy requires every citizen to take care of dependents; children, elderly, infirm, and disabled. And those on vacation. :) The design initially requires a fifty-percent dependency  membership of any mesh node. A mesh node will have about half its members be children, elderly, infirm or disabled. This builds empathy where competition of only "the best and brightest" destroys empathy required for social cohesion.
13. Vote bank. Banking votes replace casting votes. Project contracts and project objectives are voted upon using a vote bank where votes are on permanent deposit and publicly available.
14. Chain voting. Vote banks make chain voting possible. Voting blocks form as chains of votes. Votes can be deposited to use a proxy for any vote item.
15. Corruption voting. Vote banks make corruption voting possible where voters can be paid for votes as long as the payment is public.
16. Earth simulation AI. Simulation AI is used to simulate mesh project objectives over periods of time. In order to utilize the maximum number of variables possible then there will be one central AI. Initially the largest simulation will be Earth simulation AI. Solar System simulation will eventually be necessary.
17. Virtual Earth, reality you (The Very). The Very is an extension of the Earth simulation AI. The difference is everyone on Earth can enter the Very as they appear in reality. This enables hyper-socialization. Everyone on Earth can meet and interact with anyone else.
18. House AI. Each mesh node will have a house AI. This AI is simulation as well as control. This AI is analogous to the AI on Star Trek. The AI automates to the extent possible controlling systems of the mesh node. It also provides cyber-security from enemy mesh nodes.
19. Cold network. Today's Internet is referred to the hot network in New Democracy design. It is the hot network because it is real-time information. By contrast the cold network is local data in cold storage and not real-time. The cold network provides protocols for taking hot network information and sanitizing it for cold storage. This process can take days as the house AI analyses hot network data for attacks and conforms to the ethics and morals described in the mesh node charter of organization.
20. Member daily monitoring. Mesh node management required for joining projects requires daily monitoring of members. Mesh node members are required to input exercise, diet, and other daily information into a smart phone like device. This device also contains an emergency button if the member is ever threatened by the mesh node members. This monitoring provides mesh member management with the information necessary to make mesh membership decisions. These decisions are not limited to just abuse corrections but also best fit. It will be far more common for members to be moved to improve the overall effectiveness of all mesh nodes in order to optimize project objectives.

Hopefully, after reading the various parts that make up the design of the New Democracy social engineering project then you have formed ideas of your own. There are parts you reject outright and parts you can see how to improve. To which I say, welcome! This is the spirit of engineering.

The rest of this book will expand on the design of these parts and how these parts make the overall design work. Hopefully you also see that all these parts are new. These parts and the overall design represent a new frontier than can only tangentially be compared to history. This makes New Democracy a new frontier, a place to explore new social organizations. Fear and excitement are two sides of one coin. Today we are in a comfort zone of established society. We are reluctant to give that up such that things have to get physically painful to make a change. And when it does, New Democracy will be here for you.











